        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benns_Church%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "George Benn founded the church in 1789, anchoring the community's early history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benns_Church%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A Virginia Historical Marker commemorates the church’s significance in the state’s heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benns_Church%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Benns Church area grew into a 253‑acre mixed‑use development known as Benn's Grant, a project that took nearly a decade to complete.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benns_Church%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Water from Benns Church flows west to Cypress Creek, north to Jones Creek, and southeast to Brewers Creek, all feeding the James River system.",
